   308	
   309	| Revision | Date | Change | Authority |
   310	|---|---|---|---|
   311	| 1 | 2026-09-25 | Spec of record, 5 behaviours | architect |
   312	| 2 | 2026-09-25 | Sol red-team, AMEND-FIRST (7 lands / 2 held). Lands 6 and 9 changed the design; the rest corrected measurements and under-specification. Still 5 behaviours. | architect, on Sol's findings |
   313	
   314	Revision 2, land by land, each reproduced before adoption:
   315	
   316	1. **Land 1 — 12/12, not 11/12.** Ran the specified derivation over all twelve
   317	   and diffed: every one changes. My "1 of 12 usable as written" was a
   318	   subjective judgement about P-002, whose `#` the strip removes, so it changes
   319	   too. The row is replaced with a measured one and the subjective claim is
   320	   gone. Sol independently reproduced the other three measurements (six wrap
   321	   cuts, seven markdown leaks, 152/152/146).
   322	2. **Land 2 — behaviour 3 was impossible.** `needsYou()` exposes only
   323	   `state: needs_you`; P-013 is `resolved` and **P-012 is the only `needs_you`
   324	   petitio**. The behaviour now builds a temp officina or asserts P-012, and
   325	   acceptance 3 names P-012.
   326	3. **Land 4 — `body` is required.** An optional field the server always sends
   327	   is a lie in the type. Three fixtures omit it today
   328	   (`api.test.ts:63`, `inboxview.test.ts:56-57`, measured) and gain `body: ""`;
   329	   the placeholder branch is asserted directly instead of via "this test file
   330	   is untouched".
   331	4. **Lands 5 and 6 together — the design change.** P-004's first paragraph
   332	   ends `It fired.`, and a 120-char cap drops exactly that, inverting "a rule
   333	   fired, rule on it" into "a proposal to build rules". No derivation fixes
   334	   that; the information is in the second sentence. So `subject:` becomes
   335	   **required for new petitiones** with the derivation demoted to a labelled
   336	   **legacy fallback**, and the key's semantics are pinned: present-and-invalid
   337	   blocks, absent advises — `petitio.opened`'s exact two-level shape
   338	   (`check.ts:625,628`), no new pattern, and a malformed key is never rescued
   339	   by the fallback.
   340	5. **Land 7 — the algorithm is pinned.** All twelve expected strings are
   341	   asserted exactly, not just properties; the cap is **120 total including the
   342	   ellipsis** (the reference run's 120-char P-010 output is called out as the
   343	   pre-correction value); and `_`/`*` stripping is delimiter-aware, so
   344	   `snake_case` survives. No first paragraph on disk has an identifier
   345	   underscore today (measured) — the rule exists so the first one does not
   346	   corrupt silently.
   347	6. **Land 8 — `docs/ADOPTION.md` is owned unconditionally.** `:465` contracts
   348	   the body as "The question, in one paragraph", which behaviour 3 contradicts.
   349	   Revision 1 owned that file only conditionally.
   350	7. **Land 9 — the CSS line is withdrawn.** Sol held the justification but
   351	   called it unproved. I checked why it cannot be proved: no `getComputedStyle`
   352	   anywhere in `apps/web/test` or `apps/web/src`, those tests render HTML
   353	   strings, and the only DOM harness is Playwright under `test:e2e`, outside
   354	   the chain. Rather than ship a CSS change no behaviour pins, the opus becomes
   355	   purely server-side — which makes its "no UI decision" claim literally true.
   356	8. **Held 3 — the client-half claims verified** at all three cited locations.
   357	   That was revision 1's load-bearing scope argument and it stands.

